WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.321
Learn to generate and analyse patterns in square numbers and represent square numbers

00:00:05.321 --> 00:00:06.109
using factors

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:13.196
Continue the square-number sequence: 289, 324, blank . The answer is 361. Square

00:00:13.196 --> 00:00:18.961
numbers are 1 times 1, 2 times 2, 3 times 3, .

00:00:19.783 --> 00:00:25.642
A pattern uses square tiles: 1, 4, 9, 16, ... Which number represents a 12 by 12

00:00:25.642 --> 00:00:28.743
square? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:34.737
The answer is 144. 12 squared equals 144.
